  "7521556725364318208": {
   "created": 1793278867,
   "author": "Hosun Chung",
   "url": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/hosun-chung_in-2011-peter-thiel-started-paying-young-activity-7521556725364318208-qAlR",
   "text": "In 2011, Peter Thiel started paying young people $100,000 to skip college.\n17 of those fellows went on to found companies worth a combined $1.38T. 1 of them co-founded Anthropic.\nHere's the Thiel Fellowship mafia, ranked by value:\n\n1. Anthropic, $965B. Chris Olah. The AI lab behind Claude.\n2. Ethereum, $284B. Vitalik Buterin. Value of all ether.\n3. Cognition, $48B. Walden Yan. AI coding agents.\n4. Scale AI, $29B. Lucy Guo. Data for AI models.\n5. Etched, $21B. Gavin Uberti, Robert Wachen and Chris Zhu. AI inference chips.\n6. Figma, $13.1B. Dylan Field. Design software.\n7. Mercor, $10B. Brendan Foody, Adarsh Hiremath and Surya Midha. Experts for AI labs.\n8. OYO, $2.4B. Ritesh Agarwal. Budget h",
   "disc_score": 2,
